# reward-redemption-service — environment template.
#
# Copy to .env.development (or .env.test) for local work and fill in real values there — never
# commit that copy (repo root .gitignore already excludes .env / .env.* / !.env.example).
# src/config/config.schema.ts (T-RR-004) is the authoritative, validated schema for the first
# section below; this file documents intent for every var this service needs, following the same
# base/DB/Kafka/gRPC-TLS-validated-by-schema-then-everything-else-read-directly-by-its-own-module
# split RAP's own `.env.example` uses in spirit (07-CONFIGURABILITY-AND-OBSERVABILITY.md §1) —
# this service's own split additionally validates the inbound gRPC server's mTLS material here
# too (T-RR-004 implementation note 2), rather than deferring it to T-RR-011 the way RAP defers
# its own equivalent vars to T-RAP-022.
#
# Every var named here comes directly from that design doc's §1 table — nothing invented.

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3030

# --- Inbound gRPC ingestion server (T-RR-011, RewardIngestService.SubmitRewardEntry) — listen
# port + mTLS material, validated by src/config/config.schema.ts from Wave 0 onward even though
# the server itself isn't wired up until Wave 1, so a missing/malformed value fails boot loudly
# rather than surfacing only once T-RR-011 lands. Same shape as RAP's own inbound
# ActivityIngestService.
#   GRPC_SERVER_PORT                50081 (distinct from RAP's inbound 50071 and RAP's own
#                                    outbound default for calling *this* service,
#                                    REWARD_REDEMPTION_GRPC_PORT=50061 — see BACKLOG.md on that
#                                    mismatch).
#   GRPC_SERVER_TLS_CA_PATH         filesystem path to the CA cert used to verify client certs
#   GRPC_SERVER_TLS_CERT_PATH       this server's own TLS certificate
#   GRPC_SERVER_TLS_KEY_PATH        this server's own TLS private key
#   GRPC_SERVER_ALLOWED_IDENTITIES  comma-separated "identity:tenantId" entries, e.g.
#                                   "rap-ingest-client:1,other-client:2"
GRPC_SERVER_PORT=50081
GRPC_SERVER_TLS_CA_PATH=
GRPC_SERVER_TLS_CERT_PATH=
GRPC_SERVER_TLS_KEY_PATH=
GRPC_SERVER_ALLOWED_IDENTITIES=

# --- Database: the `reward_redemption` schema on the EXISTING `reward_system` Postgres 16
# server (root CLAUDE.md — /Library/PostgreSQL/16 — do NOT point this at a second, new Postgres
# instance). Two roles, the same split the portal and both sibling services already use:
#   DB_APP_*        least-privilege runtime role this service's own code connects as
#                    (`rr_app`, scoped to the `reward_redemption` schema only —
#                    AGENT-PROTOCOL.md R5). T-RR-003's own migration is what actually creates
#                    this role AND sets its login password to this value — not just a
#                    placeholder the app reads at boot. Rotate here, then re-run
#                    `npm run db:migrate` once that migration exists.
#   DB_MIGRATION_*  privileged role the migration CLI (`npm run db:migrate`/`db:rollback`)
#                    uses — never imported into request-time application code.
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=reward_system
DB_SSL=false

DB_APP_USERNAME=rr_app
DB_APP_PASSWORD=

DB_MIGRATION_USERNAME=postgres
DB_MIGRATION_PASSWORD=

# --- Kafka: comma-separated host:port broker list, for both the inbound
# `reward.entry.created.v1` consumer (T-RR-012) and the outbound
# `reward.redemption.completed.v1` producer (T-RR-034). `localhost:9094` matches this service's
# own docker-compose.yml (Redpanda) — deliberately not 9092/9093, already used by
# promo-code-service's and realtime-activity-processing-service's own local Redpanda on this
# machine (see docker-compose.yml's header).
KAFKA_BROKERS=localhost:9094

# =================================================================================================
# Everything below this line is read directly from `process.env` by its own module, NOT
# validated by src/config/config.schema.ts (each var's own owning module documents why once it
# exists — in short, config.schema.ts is agent-rr-foundation's file scope, but each of these vars
# is introduced by a later Wave 1+ task owned by a different agent). This section exists purely
# so a fresh environment has one place that names every var this service reads, matching
# config.schema.ts's own set above in spirit (AGENT-PROTOCOL.md R1 — no default secret
# committed). Values left empty are required with no default (boot fails loudly if
# unset/invalid, per each owning module's own contract); values pre-filled are the code's own
# documented default, shown here only for discoverability, not because setting it below is
# required.
# =================================================================================================

# --- Portal gRPC client + cached campaign/tracker/reward config feed (06-CACHING-AND-TENANT-
# CONFIG.md §1) — this service's outbound connection to the portal's own campaign_config.v1
# gRPC service, the same feed RAP already reads.
#   PORTAL_GRPC_HOST          defaults to localhost
#   PORTAL_GRPC_PORT          defaults to 50051 (the portal's own GRPC_DEFAULT_PORT)
#   PORTAL_GRPC_TIMEOUT_MS    defaults to 5000
#   PORTAL_GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH   mTLS client cert material. All three TLS_* vars must be set
#   PORTAL_GRPC_TLS_CERT_PATH together, or none of them (a partial set fails boot); when none
#   PORTAL_GRPC_TLS_KEY_PATH  are set this client connects over an insecure channel.
#   PORTAL_CONFIG_TENANT_IDS  required, comma-separated tenant ids this instance manages, e.g. "1,2"
PORTAL_GRPC_HOST=localhost
PORTAL_GRPC_PORT=50051
PORTAL_GRPC_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
PORTAL_GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH=
PORTAL_GRPC_TLS_CERT_PATH=
PORTAL_GRPC_TLS_KEY_PATH=
PORTAL_CONFIG_TENANT_IDS=

# --- T-INT-012: REST fallback transport + resolver for the same portal campaign-config client
# above (portal-config-rest.client.ts / portal-config-channel-resolver.service.ts). Table
# reward_redemption.portal_config_channel_config (migration 025) resolves REST vs GRPC at call
# time, GLOBAL row defaulting to REST (Render's free tier can't run gRPC yet) —
# reward-service-integration-plan/TRANSPORT-CONFIG.md's "portal-config" leg for this service. An
# explicit direct port of RAP's own identical env vars (T-INT-011), confirmed by direct read.
#   PORTAL_REST_BASE_URL                optional, defaults to http://localhost:3001/api/v1
#   PORTAL_REST_API_TOKEN               required only when the REST channel is actually attempted
#                                        (primary or fallback) — must match the portal's own
#                                        CAMPAIGN_CONFIG_API_TOKEN. No default (R1/R4 — no secret
#                                        default ships in this file).
#   PORTAL_REST_SERVICE_IDENTITY        required only when the REST channel is actually attempted
#                                        — the service_identity granted to this instance in the
#                                        portal's own grpc_service_grants table (the same table
#                                        gRPC already reads, just named via a header instead of a
#                                        certificate SAN).
#   PORTAL_REST_TIMEOUT_MS              optional, defaults to 5000
#   PORTAL_CONFIG_CHANNEL_CACHE_TTL_MS  optional, defaults to 60000 (one minute) — how long the
#                                        resolved primary/fallback channel is cached before the
#                                        next portal_config_channel_config re-read.
PORTAL_REST_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1
PORTAL_REST_API_TOKEN=
PORTAL_REST_SERVICE_IDENTITY=
PORTAL_REST_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
PORTAL_CONFIG_CHANNEL_CACHE_TTL_MS=60000

# --- promo-code-service gRPC client (T-RR-080) — the gRPC transport variant of
# `PromoCodeServiceConnector`'s existing REST call, used only when a `promo_code_channel_config`
# row resolves a `GRPC` primary channel for a given redemption (migration 018). Auth is mTLS, not
# a bearer token (see `promo-code-service-grpc.client.ts`'s own header for why this deviates from
# reusing `GENERATION_SERVICE_TOKEN`) — same "all three TLS_* vars together, or none" convention as
# PORTAL_GRPC_* above; when none are set this client connects over an insecure channel (safe only
# because promo-code-service's real gRPC server enforces mTLS at the handshake itself and will
# simply refuse an unauthenticated connection, never accept one).
#   PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_HOST          defaults to localhost
#   PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_PORT          defaults to 50061 (promo-code-service's own gRPC port)
#   PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TIMEOUT_MS    defaults to 5000
#   PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH   mTLS client cert material. All three TLS_* vars must be
#   PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TLS_CERT_PATH set together, or none of them (a partial set fails boot);
#   PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TLS_KEY_PATH  when none are set this client connects insecurely.
PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_HOST=localhost
PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_PORT=50061
PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH=
PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TLS_CERT_PATH=
PROMO_CODE_SERVICE_GRPC_TLS_KEY_PATH=

# --- reward-tracking-service gRPC client (T-RR-062) — the third dispatch-tier transport
# alongside Kafka (T-RR-034)/REST (T-RR-035), used only when a `dispatch_channel_config` row
# resolves a `GRPC` primary/fallback channel for a given redemption (migration 021, `grpc_enabled`
# defaults false everywhere). No auth mechanism is named for this channel by any design doc (unlike
# promo-code-service's own gRPC port above) — same "all three TLS_* vars together, or none"
# convention regardless; when none are set this client connects over an insecure channel.
#   REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_HOST          defaults to localhost
#   REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_PORT          defaults to 50071
#   REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TIMEOUT_MS    defaults to 5000
#   REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH   optional mTLS client cert material. All three TLS_* vars
#   REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TLS_CERT_PATH must be set together, or none of them (a partial set fails
#   REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TLS_KEY_PATH  boot); when none are set this client connects insecurely.
REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_HOST=localhost
REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_PORT=50071
REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TLS_CA_PATH=
REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TLS_CERT_PATH=
REWARD_TRACKING_GRPC_TLS_KEY_PATH=

# --- Field encryption (T-RR-005, encryption module) — AES-256-GCM + HMAC-SHA-256 for
# `customerId` at rest (AGENT-PROTOCOL.md R8), a direct port of RAP's own encryption module.
# Both required, both base64-encoded, must be different values. No default — a missing/invalid
# key crashes the process at module construction.
#   FIELD_ENCRYPTION_AES_KEY   decodes to exactly 32 bytes (AES-256-GCM's own fixed key size)
#   FIELD_ENCRYPTION_HMAC_KEY  decodes to at least 32 bytes, independent key material from the AES key
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_AES_KEY=
FIELD_ENCRYPTION_HMAC_KEY=

# --- This service's four distinct bearer tokens (R9 — never the same value as one another,
# never collapsed into a single shared secret):
#   REWARD_ENTRY_INGEST_TOKEN   guards inbound POST /api/v1/reward-entries (T-RR-013,
#                               04-REST-CONTRACT.md §1)
#   CACHE_ADMIN_TOKEN           guards POST /api/v1/cache/invalidate (T-RR-007,
#                               06-CACHING-AND-TENANT-CONFIG.md §3)
#   GENERATION_SERVICE_TOKEN    this service's own outbound credential presented to
#                               promo-code-service's POST /api/v1/promo-codes/generate
#                               (T-RR-031, ARCHITECTURE.md §8) — never this service's own
#                               inbound token, and never confused with the outbound feed
#                               described in ARCHITECTURE.md §9.
#   REWARD_TRACKING_REST_TOKEN  this service's own outbound bearer credential for the tier-2 REST
#                               fallback call to reward-tracking-service's
#                               POST /api/v1/redemptions/completed (T-RR-035,
#                               04-REST-CONTRACT.md §3) — read directly by
#                               reward-tracking-rest.client.ts's loadRewardTrackingRestToken(),
#                               not validated by config.schema.ts (same convention as the other
#                               three tokens above). Required with no default; a missing/blank
#                               value throws MissingRewardTrackingRestTokenError at
#                               RewardTrackingRestClient construction time (T-RR-066).
REWARD_ENTRY_INGEST_TOKEN=
CACHE_ADMIN_TOKEN=
GENERATION_SERVICE_TOKEN=
REWARD_TRACKING_REST_TOKEN=

# --- reward-tracking-service tier-2 REST fallback transport details (T-RR-035,
# reward-tracking-rest.client.ts) — unlike REWARD_TRACKING_REST_TOKEN above, both of these already
# have a safe code-level default (shown below), so leaving them unset is fine; set them here only
# to point this instance at a non-default reward-tracking-service host or a shorter/longer
# per-call timeout.
#   REWARD_TRACKING_REST_BASE_URL      defaults to http://localhost:4040
#   REWARD_TRACKING_REST_TIMEOUT_MS    defaults to 5000
REWARD_TRACKING_REST_BASE_URL=
REWARD_TRACKING_REST_TIMEOUT_MS=

# --- Inbound gRPC server on/off switch (T-RR-011, grpc-server.config.ts) — read directly, not
# validated by config.schema.ts. Rollback lever: set to "false" to disable the gRPC transport
# entirely (grpc-server.main.ts then never starts a listener) without touching any other config.
# Any value other than the literal string "false" — including leaving it unset — is treated as
# enabled, matching KAFKA_CONSUMER_ENABLED's own convention.
#   GRPC_SERVER_ENABLED   defaults to true (enabled) — for grpc-server.main.ts run standalone.
#
# T-INT-004: `src/main.ts`'s own hybrid bootstrap reads this SAME env var but with the OPPOSITE
# unset-default — there, only the literal string "true" starts the gRPC transport; unset (or any
# other value) leaves it off. See `src/main.ts`'s own header for why the hybrid process
# deliberately does not inherit this standalone file's "unset = enabled" convention (in short:
# Render's today-deployed hybrid process has no confirmed-valid mTLS material for this transport,
# and starting it by an "unset = on" default would crash the whole process, taking `/health` with
# it). Set to "true" only once real TLS material is in place for the hybrid process specifically.
GRPC_SERVER_ENABLED=

# --- Kafka consumer on/off switch (T-RR-012, kafka-consumer.main.ts) — read directly, not
# validated by config.schema.ts. Rollback lever: set to "false" to disable the
# `reward.entry.created.v1` consumer entirely (kafka-consumer.main.ts then never opens a broker
# connection) without touching any other config. Any value other than the literal string "false"
# — including leaving it unset — is treated as enabled, when that file is run standalone.
#   KAFKA_CONSUMER_ENABLED   defaults to true (enabled) — for kafka-consumer.main.ts run standalone.
#
# T-INT-004: `src/main.ts`'s own hybrid bootstrap reads this SAME env var but with the OPPOSITE
# unset-default — there, only the literal string "true" starts the Kafka consumer; unset (or any
# other value) leaves it off, for the identical "don't crash Render's unconfigured hybrid process
# by an unset=on default" reasoning `GRPC_SERVER_ENABLED` above documents.
KAFKA_CONSUMER_ENABLED=

# --- Claim-worker/processing/dispatch pipeline on/off switch (T-RR-058, claim-worker.module.ts) —
# read directly, not validated by config.schema.ts. Rollback lever: set to "false" to stop
# claiming/processing `reward_redemption_entry` rows entirely, without touching any other config.
# Any value other than the literal string "false" — including leaving it unset — is treated as
# enabled, when the standalone `claim-worker.main.ts` (T-RR-058) is run directly, or a dedicated
# Render `worker` service (render.yaml) runs it.
#   CLAIM_WORKER_ENABLED   defaults to true (enabled) — for claim-worker.main.ts run standalone,
#                          or the dedicated Render worker service that runs it unconditionally.
#
# T-INT-047: `src/main.ts`'s own hybrid bootstrap reads this SAME env var but with the OPPOSITE
# unset-default — there, only the literal string "true" folds `ClaimWorkerModule` (and the
# `CompletionSweepService` it transitively brings in) into this hybrid process; unset (or any other
# value) leaves it off, for the identical "don't crash Render's unconfigured hybrid process by an
# unset=on default" reasoning `GRPC_SERVER_ENABLED`/`KAFKA_CONSUMER_ENABLED` above document. Local/
# dev convenience only — the deployed shape is the dedicated Render worker service above, which
# runs this pipeline unconditionally and does not need this var set at all.
CLAIM_WORKER_ENABLED=

# --- promo-code.generate.result.v1 Kafka reply-consumer on/off switch (T-INT-053, src/main.ts's
# own hybrid bootstrap) — read directly, not validated by config.schema.ts. Rollback lever: leave
# unset (or "false") to keep this consumer from ever opening a broker connection.
# PromoCodeServiceKafkaClient.start() (T-RR-081, src/modules/connectors/promo-code-service-kafka.
# client.ts) was never called from any real running process before this task — a real, fast,
# successful reply from promo-code-service was never received, so every Kafka-primary
# rr-to-promo-code redemption exhausted its full retry budget and reached `failed` even on a
# first-attempt success (this task's own "Evidence" section, tasks/T-INT-053-*.md).
#   PROMO_CODE_KAFKA_REPLY_CONSUMER_ENABLED   defaults to false (disabled) — only the literal
#                                              string "true" starts this consumer, same
#                                              opposite-of-standalone-default convention as
#                                              GRPC_SERVER_ENABLED/KAFKA_CONSUMER_ENABLED/
#                                              CLAIM_WORKER_ENABLED above.
#
# REQUIRES `CLAIM_WORKER_ENABLED=true` in this SAME process — this consumer is resolved from the
# exact same DI graph instance `CLAIM_WORKER_ENABLED` constructs (`src/main.ts`'s own header has
# the full reasoning: the pending-reply registry this class keeps is in-memory, per-instance state,
# and the only caller of `requestAndAwaitReply()` in this service only ever runs inside
# `ClaimWorkerModule`). Setting this "true" with `CLAIM_WORKER_ENABLED` left off (or "false") makes
# `startHybridBootstrap()` reject with a clear, explicit error rather than silently starting a
# consumer that can never resolve anything.
#
# Known, disclosed gap (this task's own completion report): Render's real, always-on deployment
# shape for the claim-worker pipeline is the dedicated Render `worker` service below
# (`claim-worker.main.ts`, T-INT-047), not this hybrid gate — and `claim-worker.main.ts` is outside
# this task's own "Files owned" list, so this fix does not yet reach that topology. This gate
# covers exactly the same scope `CLAIM_WORKER_ENABLED` above covers: local/dev convenience, and the
# one topology this defect's own evidence was gathered against (a real, hybrid-bootstrapped local
# process).
PROMO_CODE_KAFKA_REPLY_CONSUMER_ENABLED=
